<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch January consumer prices rise 2.3 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Dutch January consumer prices rise 2.3 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>VOORBURG, Netherlands 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Dutch consumer price index (CPI) rose a provisional 0.3 percent in January from December, giving a 2.3 percent year-on-year rise, the Central Bureau of Statistics (CBS) said.  </p>
<p>DUTCH CONSUMER PRICE INFLATION   Jan 97	Dec 96     Jan 96</p>
<p> Monthly CPI pct change		 0.3	 -0.1	  0.4</p>
<p> Year-on-year CPI pct change	  2.3	  2.5	  1.9</p>
<p> Index (base 1990)		    118.0	117.7	115.3</p>
<p>NOTES - Economists polled by Reuters had expected the January CPI to rise between 2.3 percent and 2.7 percent year-on-year, with a consensus at 2.5 percent.  </p>
<p>The detailed index figures were:</p>
<p>					    Weighting    Jan 97    Dec 96</p>
<p> Food, drink, tobacco			 180     111.7     109.8</p>
<p> Clothes, shoes				  72	87.0	97.9</p>
<p> Rent, heating, lighting		    261     132.5     131.1</p>
<p> Furniture, household appliances etc.    80     106.8     107.0</p>
<p> Medical care				     6     119.5     119.3</p>
<p> Transport, communication		   144     119.9     119.2</p>
<p> Leisure, education			   107     109.1     107.6</p>
<p> Other goods, services			113     116.4     116.0</p>
<p> Consumer taxes, govt. services	    37     154.7     151.0</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
